Alembic migrations for the School Results Portal.

Every schema change ships as a migration (CLAUDE.md rule 3).  Never edit a model
without generating and reviewing the migration, and never hand-edit the database.

    docker compose exec api alembic upgrade head
    docker compose exec api alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..."
    docker compose exec api alembic current
    docker compose exec api alembic downgrade -1

The database URL comes from app.config.settings, never from alembic.ini.

Revision ids are sequential and explicit (0001, 0002, ...) because this is a
single-branch repository and readable history is worth more than collision
resistance.  Pass the next number when creating a revision:

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add core schema" --rev-id 0002

Migrations are an explicit deploy step and never run at container start
(ARCHITECTURE.md §11).
